# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed — this is an application, not a library.
# (see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-16-animus-live-design.md §15.2)

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Build & release artifacts
/dist/
/out/
*.zip
*.msi
*.exe

# Local scratch
/scratch/
/spikes/**/target/

# Test output
/tests/output/
**/snapshots/*.snap.new
spikes/target/

# Third-party test assets are kept outside this repository (they live in
# ../animus-demo-files) because their terms do not all permit
# redistribution. This entry is a guard in case any land here again.
/demo-files/

# Saved shows. A `.animus` bundle is a *document* — someone's artwork and
# their rig — and it belongs to whoever made it, not to this repository.
# Committing one would put an artist's character into the project history,
# where taking it back out again is far harder than never adding it.
*.animus/

# Design comps live beside the repo rather than in it: they are bundled
# exports measured in hundreds of kilobytes and they change on every
# revision, so the history would be mostly comp.
/claude design/
